## Dependency Security Overlays

HolyClaude replaces selected compatible dependency copies with version-pinned
archives and fail-closed path checks. Overlays that replace a known vendored copy
also verify its owning tool and original dependency version before changing it.
v1.6.0 includes overlays for selected copies of setuptools, Piscina, brace-expansion,
js-yaml, minimatch, Nanoid, path-to-regexp, Sharp, smol-toml, Undici, ws, and xmldom. The full
image uses js-yaml 4.3.2 in PM2 and Vercel, and Sharp 0.35.4 with matching
native bindings and libvips package 1.3.3 in Wrangler and Netlify. Vercel uses
smol-toml 1.7.1. Marp's speech-rule-engine
uses xmldom 0.9.12; EAS's separate xmldom 0.8.15 copy is unchanged. CloudCLI retains its
separate js-yaml 3.15.2 overlay. Cursor Agent uses
HolyClaude's Node 26.8.2 runtime instead of its bundled Node binary.

These packages retain their upstream licenses. The exact versions, archive
hashes, owning paths, and fail-closed patch checks are recorded in the
Dockerfile, `security/immutable-inputs.yml`, and the release source.

